I've successfully viewed IBMgraphics NetHack using Unix PuTTY. I did
it by the use of a Unicode font: bring up the Unix PuTTY font
selector and see if you can find a font which has an `iso10646-1'
option in the Font Style box. Select that as PuTTY's main font, and
pick CP437 as the character set in the Translation panel, and see if
that works.

If your system doesn't have any Unicode fonts installed,
http://www.cl.cam.ac.uk/~mgk25/unicode.html#fonts has a number of
links which might help you get hold of some.

(The alternative to a full-Unicode font for this purpose is a CP437
or CP850 one. There might be such X fonts generally available
_somewhere_, but the only one I've actually seen was one I
constructed myself for a special purpose.)
